  "question": {
    "html": "<p>A stone of mass <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"m\"></span> is dropped into a tube containing a liquid of specific heat capacity <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"c\"></span>. The stone falls through a vertical distance of <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"H\"></span> and <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"75\"></span> % of its initial gravitational potential energy is converted into kinetic energy. The rest of the initial gravitational potential energy is absorbed by the liquid. As a result, the temperature of the liquid increases by <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"T\"></span>. What is the mass of the liquid in the tube?</p>\n<p></p>\n<ol class=\"mcq-options\">\n<li data-label=\"A\"><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"\\frac{mgH}{4cT}\"></span></li>\n<li data-label=\"B\"><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"\\frac{4mgH}{cT}\"></span></li>\n<li data-label=\"C\"><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"\\frac{3mgH}{4cT}\"></span></li>\n<li data-label=\"D\"><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"\\frac{4mgH}{3cT}\"></span></li>\n</ol>"
  },
